This file contains the architecture, the flow and the proposed calculations for the FOC being worked upon.
ADC reads Ia, Ib
        ↓
Clarke Transform  →  Ialpha, Ibeta
        ↓
Park Transform    →  Id, Iq        (needs theta from encoder)
        ↓
Id PI Controller  →  Vd            (Id ref = 0 for PMSM)
Iq PI Controller  →  Vq            (Iq ref = from speed ref)
        ↓
Inverse Park      →  Valpha, Vbeta (needs theta)
        ↓
SVPWM             →  CCR1, CCR2, CCR3
        ↓
TIM1 PWM output   →  IGBT gates    →  Motor


Inputs (fake for now):

Ia, Ib — phase currents from ADC (we fake as sine waves)
theta — rotor angle from encoder (we fake as incrementing float)
speed_ref — operator speed reference

Calculated inside:

Ic = -(Ia + Ib) — Kirchhoff, no third sensor needed
Ialpha, Ibeta — after Clarke
Id, Iq — after Park
Vd, Vq — after PI controllers
Valpha, Vbeta — after Inverse Park
CCR1, CCR2, CCR3 — after SVPWM

State:

PI integrators — must persist between calls
Drive state — INIT / READY / RUNNING / FAULT


Proposed File Structure
src/
├── foc_transforms.cpp     — Clarke, Park, Inverse Park
├── pi_controller.cpp      — PI struct, calculate()
├── svpwm.cpp              — sector detection, T1/T2/T0, CCR values
├── foc_controller.cpp     — ties everything together, one foc_step() call
├── mock_hal.cpp           — fake ADC, fake encoder, fake PWM write
└── main_sim.cpp           — runs the loop, prints output

include/
├── foc_transforms.h
├── pi_controller.h
├── svpwm.h
├── foc_controller.h
└── mock_hal.h

// foc_transforms
void clarke(float Ia, float Ib, float &Ialpha, float &Ibeta);
void park(float Ialpha, float Ibeta, float theta, float &Id, float &Iq);
void inverse_park(float Vd, float Vq, float theta, float &Valpha, float &Vbeta);

// pi_controller
struct PIController { float Kp, Ki, dt, integrator, limit; };
float pi_calculate(PIController &pi, float error);

// svpwm
void svpwm(float Valpha, float Vbeta, float Vbus, uint32_t ARR,
           uint32_t &CCR1, uint32_t &CCR2, uint32_t &CCR3);

// mock_hal
float mock_adc_Ia(float theta);   // returns sin(theta)
float mock_adc_Ib(float theta);   // returns sin(theta - 2pi/3)
float mock_encoder_theta();       // advances theta each call

// foc_controller — the main orchestrator
void foc_init();
void foc_step(float speed_ref);   // one complete FOC iteration

foc_controller.cpp owns:
    PIController id_pi      — flux controller
    PIController iq_pi      — torque controller
    float theta             — current rotor angle
    float Id, Iq            — current feedback
    float Vd, Vq            — voltage commands
    float Ialpha, Ibeta     — intermediate
    float Valpha, Vbeta     — intermediate
    uint32_t CCR1,CCR2,CCR3 — output to mock PWM

All declared static — no malloc, no global pollution


